// The climate of each part of the world, as a layer stack read by weather.ClimateMap: a tile's climate is the LAST
// layer that contains it. A layer is {climate: climates.json id, areas: [117 HD area names (scene/areas.json)],
// rects: [[x1, y1, x2, y2] world tiles, inclusive], note}. Underground is decided before the layers: a tile whose
// 117 HD environment is not overworld has no climate (ClimateMap.NO_SKY), so caves, dungeons, instances and the
// other planes (Zanaris) never reach this file. "default" is the climate of an overworld tile no layer contains.
// Layers marked "guess" place regions the climate map does not list, or resolve a conflict in it.
